    <p class="statute-block__label">Primary Sources</p>
    <ul class="statute-block__list">
      <li><a href="https://www.leg.state.fl.us/statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&URL=0600-0699%2F0689%2FSections%2F0689.01.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Florida Statutes §689.01</strong></a> — deed execution and witness requirements</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.leg.state.fl.us/statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&URL=0600-0699%2F0689%2FSections%2F0689.11.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Florida Statutes §689.11</strong></a> — spouse-to-spouse conveyances and tenancy by the entireties</li>
      <li><a href="https://leg.state.fl.us/Statutes/index.cfm/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&URL=0600-0699%2F0695%2FSections%2F0695.03.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Florida Statutes §695.03</strong></a> — acknowledgment and proof of deeds for recording</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.leg.state.fl.us/statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&URL=0200-0299%2F0201%2FSections%2F0201.02.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Florida Statutes §201.02</strong></a> — documentary stamp tax on deeds</li>
      <li><a href="https://floridarevenue.com/taxes/taxesfees/Pages/doc_stamp.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Florida Department of Revenue — Documentary Stamp Tax</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="statute-block__note">Last Verified: August 2026. Laws change. Verify current requirements before recording.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="disclaimer-note"><em>This article provides general educational information, not legal, tax, or financial advice. Consult an appropriate Florida professional for advice about a specific transfer.</em></p>
